1225:	\leanok
1226:	\uses{def:line-point-dist, def:ld-question-distribution}
1227:	For any $i \in \{1, \dots, m\}$, the \emph{$i$-th restricted
1228:	axis-parallel line distribution} $D_{\mathrm{ALine},i}$ is the
1229:	restriction of $D_{\mathrm{ALine}}$ to pairs $(\ell, u)$ where the line
1230:	$\ell$ is along the direction $e_i$, i.e.\ is of the form
1231:	$\ell = (u_0, e_i)$. Similarly, the \emph{$i$-th restricted diagonal line
1232:	distribution} $D_{\mathrm{DLine},i}$ is the restriction of
1233:	$D_{\mathrm{DLine}}$ to pairs $(\ell, u)$ where the line
1234:	$\ell = (u_0, s, v)$ satisfies $\chi(s) = i$ and coordinates
1235:	$1, \dots, i-1$ of $v$ are $0$. (The function $\chi$ is the one used in
1236:	the question distribution of the low individual degree game,
1237:	Definition~\ref{def:ld-question-distribution}.)
